SUMMARY
Complex APT intrusion with lateral movement, C2, and exfiltration that automated tools did not catch. Hunters must surface this activity proactively — a direct test of the 'assume breach' hunting philosophy.

SOURCE
https://kc7cyber.com/challenges/26

STEPS TAKEN
Section 1: KQL 101
Do a take 10 on the Employees table. Which column contains email data?
Employees
| take 10
Answer: email_addr

How many employees are in the company?
Employees
| count
Answer: 729

Which employee has the IP address: “192.168.2.191”? (provide the name)
Employees
| where ip_addr == "192.168.2.191"
Answer: Ronald Walker

How many emails did Ronald Walker receive?
let ronald_email=
Employees
| where name == "Ronald Walker"
| project email_addr;
Email
| where recipient in (ronald_email)
| count
Answer: 15

How many Balloons Over Iowa employees received emails with the term "ufos" in the subject?
Email
| where subject has "ufos"
| where recipient has "iowaballoons.com"
| distinct recipient
Answer: 441

How many unique websites did Jorge Hardwick visit?
let jorge_ip=
Employees
| where name == "Jorge Hardwick"
| project ip_addr;
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip in (jorge_ip)
| distinct url
| count
Answer: 11

How many distinct domains in the PassiveDns records contain the word “infiltrate”?
PassiveDns
| where domain contains "infiltrate"
| distinct domain
| count
Answer: 7

What IP did the domain cheeseburger-infiltrate.com resolve to on February 8th?
PassiveDns
| where domain == "cheeseburger-infiltrate.com"
Answer: 40.208.15.1

How many distinct URLs were browsed by employees with the first name Karen?
let karen_ips=
Employees
| where name has "Karen"
| distinct ip_addr;
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip in (karen_ips)
| distinct url
Answer: 27


